nethack.alt.org, after much laziness on my part, is finally upgraded
to nethack 3.4.3. Savegames and bonesfiles have been tested and work
just fine.

We're also running on the new dgamelaunch 1.4.something, which
features sending mail to players in game (via the mail daemon of
course). This can be done while watching the games in the dgamelaunch
wrapper.

For those that haven't played on nethack.alt.org, it is a public
server that allows watching of all games in realtime, playing (of
course), saving of all tty sessions for later viewing by all, full
editing of nethackrc files, and now communication with players via
in-game mail. (Thanks to the jilles/joshk simplemail patch) It is
located in San Jose, CA, USA, so is very low latency to the US, and
even reasonably low latencies at various other spots worldwide. EU
players might also want to try the fishpool.fi server.

